---
import BranchLayout from '../../layouts/BranchLayout.astro';
import BranchSteps from '../../components/BranchSteps.astro';
import GateIntro from '../../components/GateIntro.astro';
import Giscus from '../../components/Giscus.astro';
import Treatise from '../../components/Treatise.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');

const title = '神道法 · 法门介绍';

const description = '神道法门介绍：香火念力所生之法——聚念、拜神、下种、带功、灌顶、附身；神道法有四，其利在易，其弊在受制。本门所传为自力一路，此门只为辨明。';

// 正文：源文件《神道法》全篇，由 .qa/gzh-gen.mjs 机械生成，逐字未改
const chapters = [
  {
    blocks: [
      { t: 'p', text: '我这里说的神道是从神形方面去区分的内容。', en: 'The divine way I speak of here is a distinction drawn on the side of spirit and form.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '重神、单神不求肉身为神道，身形皆求为神形俱妙之道。', en: 'To prize the spirit and seek the spirit alone, not seeking the physical body — that is the divine way. To seek both body and form is the way of spirit and form both wondrous.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '神道法轻身重形，古往今来无数存在前赴后继，对于神形俱妙之道来说要方便很多。神道法从根本上来说来说也分为自力和它力体系', en: 'The divine way makes light of the body and prizes the form; down the ages countless beings have pressed forward in its wake — it is far more convenient than the way of spirit and form both wondrous. At root the divine way, too, divides into self-power and other-power systems.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '我这里自力神道、它力神道皆可传授，真有需要次路的认真思考清楚即可。', en: 'Here both the self-power and other-power divine ways can be transmitted; if you truly need this road, only think it through carefully.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '从法门上来讲，很多人都听说过的内容都是神道法门，例如：丹道、大洞、欧景等', en: 'In terms of methods, much of what people have heard of is divine-way method — elixir-path alchemy, the Great Cavern, Oujing, and the like.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '自古道法有诸多限制，但神道除了遵守不得泄规矩之外，剩下的限制较少。', en: 'Since ancient times the Dao-methods have carried many restrictions; in the divine way, apart from keeping the rule of no leaking, few restrictions remain.' },
      {
        t: 'items',
        items: [
          '1：不限制吃喝',
          '2:不限制种族（自力除外）',
          '3：不限制结婚生子',
          '4:不限制正常生活以及工作',
          '6：不限制行业，无论是上至王候将相、下至贩 夫走卒，一视同仁',
        ],
        itemsEn: [
          '1: No restriction on food and drink',
          '2: No restriction of kind (the self-power path excepted)',
          '3: No restriction on marriage and children',
          '4: No restriction on ordinary life or work',
          '6: No restriction of station — from kings, marquises, generals and ministers down to pedlars and foot-servants, all are treated alike',
        ],
      },
      { t: 'p', text: '以下为神道方面秘闻，以前都是隐秘传内容，之所以给大家讲这些，就是让大家对神道能有一定的了解。明白清楚自己选择了什么', en: 'What follows are esoteric matters of the divine way, once transmitted in strict secrecy. I set them out so that you may have some understanding of the divine way — knowing clearly what it is you have chosen.' },
    ],
  },
  {
    title: '自力修炼法门神道法体系：',
    titleEn: 'The Self-Power Divine-Way System:',
    blocks: [
      { t: 'p', text: '此路核心还是通过自己的刻苦修炼最终达到一定成就，伟力归于自己，成可遨游世间、法界，不重肉身只重神魂，汉后逐渐兴起。', en: 'At the core of this road one reaches certain attainments through one\'s own hard practice; the mighty power returns to oneself. When accomplished, one can roam the world and the dharma-realm; the body is not prized, only the spirit-soul — it rose gradually after the Han.' },
    ],
  },
  {
    title: '非自力修炼法门神道法体系：',
    titleEn: 'The Non-Self-Power Divine-Way System:',
    blocks: [
      { t: 'p', text: '第一种：是祖先神道以及祖先神道衍生出的三不朽神道和祖师神道。', en: 'The first: the ancestral divine way, and the Three Imperishables and patriarchal divine ways that derive from it.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '第二种：是封神法，汇聚万民心念成就神佛，也就是我们通常所说的香火神道；包括百姓封神、朝廷封神和立教修神。', en: 'The second: the rite of enfeoffing gods — gathering the mind-thought of the myriad people to accomplish gods and buddhas; what we usually call the incense-fire divine way. It includes enfeoffment by the common people, by the imperial court, and by founding a religion.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '第三种：是通过传播宗教，获取神道功德，死后受封成为神官。', en: 'The third: spreading religion to gain divine-way merit, and after death receiving enfeoffment as a divine official.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '第四种：是依靠附庸神明祖师仙佛，以自身神气或修炼来壮大神明种子，最终修成有一定自我意识的神佛化身。', en: 'The fourth: attaching as a vassal to gods, patriarchs, immortals or buddhas, using one\'s own spirit-qi or practice to swell the deity-seed, and at last accomplishing a god-or-buddha emanation with some degree of self-awareness.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '二三两种其实是可以重叠的，丹家所谓神仙、地仙，道上有功、人间有行、功行圆满，受诏飞升，成为天仙，其本质上就是受封神官。', en: 'The second and third can in fact overlap: what the elixir school calls immortals — earth-immortals who gain merit in the Dao and deeds among men, whose merit and deeds are complete, who receive the summons and ascend as heaven-immortals — are in essence enfeoffed divine officials.' },
    ],
  },
  {
    title: '第一种：是祖先神道以及祖先神道衍生出的三不朽神道和祖师神道。（不太合适现代修炼）',
    titleEn: 'The First: the Ancestral Divine Way, and the Three-Imperishables and Patriarchal Ways That Derive From It (not well suited to modern cultivation)',
    blocks: [
      { t: 'p', text: '祖先神道是神道的源头之一：', en: 'The ancestral divine way is one of the sources of the divine way:' },
      { t: 'p', text: '祖先神和自然神是这个世界上最早的神灵。祖先神是祖先受到后人的景仰追思汇聚而成，祖先神的力量也来源于此。', en: 'Ancestor-gods and nature-gods are the earliest deities of this world. The ancestor-god is formed from the gathered admiration and remembrance of posterity; from this too comes the ancestor-god\'s power.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '当然这也是香火心念，但属于比较纯粹，污染很小的香火心念。所以祖先神的优势就是受香火污染程度低，比较清醒。', en: 'This, of course, is also incense-fire mind-thought — but a comparatively pure kind, little polluted. So the ancestor-god\'s advantage is a low degree of incense-fire pollution: greater clarity.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '祖先与后人之间，也没有基于崇拜信仰的人神互役的弊端。', en: 'And between ancestor and descendant there is none of the drawback of mutual enslavement of man and god that rests on worship and faith.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '但它的缺点同样不小，就是法力比较弱，就算是多子多孙，也很难有标准的香火神那么多的香火供奉。', en: 'But its faults are no less great: its dharma-power is comparatively weak. Even with many sons and grandsons, it can hardly receive as much offering as a standard incense-fire god.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '而人丁稀薄的氏族，祖先神就会趋于消亡。', en: 'And in clans of thinning numbers, the ancestor-god trends toward dissolution.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '因为人丁稀薄供奉减少，或者随着世代相传，较早的祖先因只剩下名字丧失其独立性，而融合成一个“祖先”共同体。', en: 'Whether because dwindling numbers bring fewer offerings, or as generations pass: the earlier ancestors — left with nothing but names, their independence lost — merge into a single "ancestors" collective.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '为了弥补这个缺陷，人们开始用宰杀三牲或奴隶，用他们的灵魂供给祖先吞噬，来维持和增强祖先神的法力。但这种方法，对祖先的污染程度比较高，且花费比较大，一般是用不起的。', en: 'To make up for this defect, people began slaughtering the three sacrificial beasts, or slaves, feeding their souls to the ancestors to devour, so as to maintain and strengthen the ancestor-god\'s power. But this method pollutes the ancestors rather heavily and costs a great deal; ordinarily it is beyond means.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '当巫教衰弱，巫教的正统继承人儒家在去宗教化以后，讲求仁义，就更不可能大肆屠杀奴隶供养祖先。所以就衍生出了三不朽神道', en: 'When the shamanic religion waned, its orthodox heir, Confucianism, after shedding its religious character, set forth benevolence and righteousness — all the less could it slaughter slaves in great numbers to feed the ancestors. And so arose the Three-Imperishables divine way.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '就是《左传》说的人生三不朽：太上有立德，其次有立功，其次有立言，虽久不废，此之谓不朽。', en: 'This is the three imperishables of a life spoken of in the Zuo Commentary: highest is to establish virtue; next, to establish merit; next, to establish words. Though long enduring, they are not cast aside — this is called imperishability.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '改变纯粹的血脉后代供奉，通过立德立功立言的方法，让后代记住，让后代景仰追思。', en: 'Instead of offerings from blood descendants alone: through establishing virtue, merit and words, one is remembered by posterity, admired and remembered in thought.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '三不朽神道本来是很完美的神道，既解决了祖先神道的香火数量问题，又没有大的污染。', en: 'The Three-Imperishables divine way was originally a most perfect divine way: it solved the ancestor-way\'s problem of the number of offerings, and carried no great pollution.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '但立德、立功这两条，很容易在后人供奉中变质成香火神道。而且这其中只有真正优秀的人，才能永垂不朽，永远被后人铭记。', en: 'But the paths of virtue and merit easily degenerate into the incense-fire divine way amid the offerings of posterity. And of these, only the truly outstanding can remain imperishable forever, forever remembered by later generations.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '祖先神道的另一个变种就是祖师神道：', en: 'Another variant of the ancestral divine way is the patriarchal divine way:' },
      { t: 'p', text: '祖师神道基本和祖先神道是一致的，只是从血脉传承改变为技艺传承、知识传承，从而大大扩大了供奉祖师的后辈数量。', en: 'The patriarchal way is basically the same as the ancestral way, only changed from blood lineage to the transmission of craft and knowledge — greatly enlarging the number of juniors who make offering to the patriarch.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '并且祖师神道还衍生出另一条道路，就是祖师给后辈下种，吸收后辈的修炼成果，来壮大自身乃至超越自身，或者将后辈收入麾下，扩充自身在法界的势力。', en: 'And the patriarchal way has spawned another road besides: the patriarch plants a seed in the juniors, absorbing the fruits of their practice to swell himself and even surpass himself, or taking the juniors under his banner, expanding his own power in the dharma-realm.' },
    ],
  },
  {
    title: '第二种：是封神法，汇聚万民心念成就神佛，也就是我们通常所说的香火神道；包括百姓封神、朝廷封神和立教修神。（香火神道算是后世主流）',
    titleEn: 'The Second: the Rite of Enfeoffing Gods — Gathering the Mind-Thought of the Myriad People to Accomplish Gods and Buddhas, What We Usually Call the Incense-Fire Divine Way; It Includes Enfeoffment by the People, by the Court, and by Founding a Religion (the incense-fire divine way may be counted the mainstream of later ages)',
    blocks: [
      { t: 'p', text: '第二种里面，最初的香火神道是百姓封神，就是基于百姓所崇拜的自然界的各种事物，如太阳月亮大树大山，并基于他们本身的性质由香火心念赋予神职，成为香火神中的自然神，如日神月神树神山神。这之后，才出现对于各种生灵人物的崇拜，并逐渐呈现一种人格神的形态。就连自然神，也发展出现人格形态。', en: 'Within the second, the earliest incense-fire divine way was enfeoffment by the common people — based on the various things of nature they worshipped, such as the sun, the moon, great trees and great mountains; and from their own qualities, by incense-fire mind-thought, divine offices were assigned, making natural gods among the incense-fire gods: sun-god, moon-god, tree-god, mountain-god. Only afterwards did worship of various living beings and figures appear, gradually taking on a personal-god form. Even the natural gods developed personal forms.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '但在华夏，神权需要服从于王权。百姓封神不一定受到朝廷的承认，得到承认，才是正神，如果没有得到承认，就是淫祀野神。', en: 'But in Hua-Xia, divine authority must submit to kingly authority. Enfeoffment by the people is not necessarily recognized by the court; only with recognition is one a proper god. Without it, one is a licentious sacrifice, a wild god.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '像玉皇大帝这么大的道教大佬，在宋朝的时候才被朝廷正式承认，甚至一度取代昊天上帝接受朝廷祭祀。但最终仍然只是一教之尊，代表天地正统的天帝还是昊天上帝。', en: 'Even one so great as the Jade Emperor, a grandee of Daoism, was formally recognized by the court only in the Song, and for a time even replaced Haotian Shangdi in receiving the court\'s sacrifices. But in the end he is honored only as the head of one religion; the Heaven-God representing the orthodox order of heaven and earth remains Haotian Shangdi.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '朝廷获得的封神权的合法性在于其政权的合法性，政权的合法性又在于民心的认可和受命于天，古人又说过，天命即人心，还说过为天地立心这样的话。', en: 'The legitimacy of the court\'s enfeoffing power rests on the legitimacy of its regime; and the regime\'s legitimacy rests on the people\'s acceptance and on the mandate of Heaven. The ancients said the mandate of Heaven is the heart of the people, and also spoke of setting a heart for heaven and earth.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '所以朝廷的封神权归根结底还是来自于百姓，又通过政权的力量来引导百姓的信仰。', en: 'So the court\'s enfeoffing power comes in the final analysis from the people; and through the power of the regime it guides the people\'s faith.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '百姓对朝廷和皇权的认可，也是一种信力一种香火，这种香火信力赋予朝廷镇压一切神佛的实力，所以政权才被称为社稷神器。', en: 'The people\'s acceptance of court and throne is itself a faith-power, an incense-fire; and this incense-fire of faith endows the court with the power to press down all gods and buddhas — which is why the regime is called the sacred vessel of the altars of soil and grain.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '而政权的象征，例如九鼎、玉玺，也被称作社稷神器。', en: 'And the symbols of the regime — the nine tripods, the imperial seal — are likewise called sacred vessels of the altars.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '封神的圣旨，也可以说是社稷神器的代表，是皇帝和朝廷所拥有的庞大法力的认可，就可以赋予受封者神格。', en: 'An imperial edict enfeoffing a god may be called a representative of the sacred vessel: the recognition carried by the vast dharma-power the emperor and court hold, able to confer divine rank on the one enfeoffed.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '正因为具有了封神权，所以皇帝才是三界至尊，在皇帝和皇权之上的，只有一个昊天上帝和后土皇地祇，代表的是宇宙和地球。', en: 'It is precisely by holding the power of enfeoffment that the emperor is supreme in the three realms. Above emperor and throne stand only Haotian Shangdi and Houtu Huangdiqi, who represent the cosmos and the earth.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '自古以来，鬼神都是有品级的，鬼神也要敬畏高级官员和皇帝，天庭的臣子，在皇帝面前也是臣子。所以除非皇帝和高官自甘堕落崇拜鬼神（这是鬼神之道一直在努力的一个方向），鬼神是并不能靠近他们的，没有天帝神格，谁来了也得跪。', en: 'Since ancient times the ghosts and gods have ranks; ghosts and gods must also revere high officials and the emperor. The ministers of the celestial court are, before the emperor, ministers too. So unless emperor and high officials willfully stoop to worship ghosts and gods (a direction the ghost-and-god way has always striven toward), ghosts and gods cannot come near them. Without the divine rank of the Heaven-God, whoever comes must kneel.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '立教封神，是唯一一种靠自身修炼成就神位的。（难度很大，创立教派，播散信徒，专业的修炼次第等等，在一些宗教比较盛行的地方要方便一点，比如棒子等，再说什么时代了还立教？可以用别的方法办到）', en: 'Founding a religion and being enfeoffed a god is the only way to attain divine office by one\'s own practice. (Extremely difficult — founding a sect, spreading the faith, a professional order of practice, and so forth; somewhat easier in places where religion flourishes, Korea for instance. And besides, what age is this to be founding religions? Other methods can accomplish it.)' },
      { t: 'p', text: '就算修成了，神人互役的大缺陷，也是摆脱不了的。修炼成神而不是成就属神的这种神道修士，应该是以独立觉悟为目标的，但是我不认为他们最终能够摆脱香火束缚。', en: 'Even if one succeeds, the great flaw of mutual enslavement of god and man cannot be escaped. The divine-way cultivator who cultivates to become a god rather than a subordinate god ought to aim at independent awakening — but I do not think they can in the end escape the bonds of incense-fire.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '修神者首先需要有具备这其中最大的考验就是保持自身的清明，不然魂魄变成聻，即便还能回到身体，没有魂飞魄散，也会变成傻子疯子，也活不了太久。另一点是随着精神的壮大，而且这个精神又是杂乱的污染的香火集聚而成的，', en: 'The god-cultivator must first possess — and the greatest trial in this is — keeping his own clarity. Otherwise the soul becomes a jian: even if it can return to the body, not scattered to the winds, one becomes a fool or a madman, and does not live long. Another point: as the spirit swells — and this spirit is gathered together from tangled, polluted incense-fire —' },
      { t: 'p', text: '但修神者死后仍然是香火汇聚的对象，所以只要所立宗教不出问题，就能够死后封神。现在信息传播迅速，立教之外有了其他选择，例如歌星演员等名人，都可以借助这个方法修炼，死后封神，但如果名声不能持续，就会跌下神坛，化为鬼聻，连阴神都不如。这其中有一种误解，是认为只要名声大信力多死后就能封神，而不知道里面也是有一定门道的。', en: 'But the god-cultivator, after death, remains an object where incense-fire gathers; so long as the religion he founded does not fail, he can be enfeoffed a god after death. With information now spreading so swiftly, there are choices beyond founding a religion: singers, actors and other celebrities can cultivate by this method too and be enfeoffed after death — but if the fame cannot endure, they fall from the altar and become ghost-jian, lower even than a shade-god. There is a misunderstanding here: that great fame and much faith-power suffice for deification after death, not knowing that there is a certain art within it as well.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '所以说，各种封神法封神，有的纯粹是万民心念，有的万民心念加上本人魂魄，有的是万民心念加残魂，有的只是万民心念加上聚集已消散者的留世痕迹。但他们自己，如果有那么一点意识的话，都是坚定认为自己就是那个生前的本人的。', en: 'Thus in the various enfeoffments: some are purely the mind-thought of the myriad people; some are that mind-thought plus the person\'s own soul; some, the mind-thought plus a remnant soul; some merely the mind-thought plus the gathered traces left in the world by one long dissolved. But they themselves, if they have even a shred of awareness, firmly hold that they are that very person from before death.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '也许有的积年老神突然意识到自己不是那个人，我觉得也有可能。至于有没有魂魄能保持完全独立，利用香火而不沾香火，那是不存在的。', en: 'Perhaps some old god of long standing suddenly realizes he is not that person — I think it possible. As to whether a soul can remain wholly independent, using incense-fire without being touched by it — no such thing exists.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '另外，修炼神道成就的神如果违背了众生之念的话，就相当于叛离了自己存在的基础，就会引发香火的反噬，影响自我意识，乃至被香火排斥分裂出来，下场凄惨。', en: 'Moreover, if a god accomplished through the divine way goes against the mind-thought of living beings, that is to betray the very basis of his existence: it triggers the backlash of incense-fire, affects his self-awareness, and may even split him off, cast out by the incense-fire — a wretched end.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '但想违背集体意志，也不是那么容易的，起码是对自身意志和万民香火控制力都达到很强的程度才有可能。', en: 'But to defy the collective will is not so easy: it takes great strength of both one\'s own will and one\'s control of the people\'s incense-fire even to be possible.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '（二三两种其实是可以重叠的，丹家所谓神仙、地仙，道上有功、人间有行、功行圆满，受诏飞升，成为天仙，其本质上就是受封神官。）', en: '(The second and third can overlap: what the elixir school calls immortals — earth-immortals, who gain merit in the Dao and deeds among men, whose merit and deeds are complete, who receive the summons and ascend as heaven-immortals — are in essence enfeoffed divine officials.)' },
    ],
  },
  {
    title: '第三种：是通过传播宗教，获取神道功德，死后受封成为神官。',
    titleEn: 'The Third: Spreading Religion to Gain Divine-Way Merit, and After Death to Be Enfeoffed a Divine Official.',
    blocks: [
      { t: 'p', text: '通过宗教功德被封神官或者仆神的，无论权柄还是神炁，皆来自于神明封赐。无论意识还是法力，都是予取予夺。但这也是最简单的长生法，如果认为那种状态能算长生的话。', en: 'For those enfeoffed as divine officials or servant-gods through religious merit: authority and spirit-qi alike come as grants from the deity. Consciousness and dharma-power alike are given and taken away at will. Yet this is also the simplest method of long life — if that state can be counted long life at all.' },
    ],
  },
  {
    title: '第四种：依靠附庸神明祖师仙佛，以自身神气或修炼来壮大神明种子，最终修成有一定自我意识的神佛化身。',
    titleEn: 'The Fourth: Depending on Gods, Patriarchs, Immortals or Buddhas as a Vassal, Using One\'s Own Spirit-Qi or Practice to Swell the Deity-Seed, and at Last Accomplishing a God-or-Buddha Emanation with Some Self-Awareness.',
    blocks: [
      { t: 'p', text: '是有很大一部分自力修炼成分的，甚至于有纯靠自力修练也能成道的法门，但由于身上有种子或附体，依附于神佛祖师，所以只能算神道修炼。虽然是半自力，但神道和自力修炼之间非此即彼，没有中间路线。', en: 'There is a large component of self-power practice in it — there are even methods of pure self-power that can reach the Way — but because a seed or a possessing spirit is present, because one clings to gods, buddhas and patriarchs, it can only be counted divine-way cultivation. Though half self-power, between the divine way and self-power practice it is either one or the other; there is no middle road.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '香火这个东西，无论是受供者还是供奉者，修为不到一定程度，就像毒药一下，沾上就会入神道。并不只有跳大神烧香磕头才叫迷信啊，灌顶下种乃至神佛观想，都是神道修法。不止如此，你虔诚信仰，也会获得神明种子。', en: 'Incense-fire — whether for the one receiving or the one making offering — unless one\'s attainment reaches a certain degree, is like poison: touch it, and you enter the divine way. It is not only shaman-dancing, incense-burning and kowtowing that count as superstition: empowerment, seed-planting, and even visualization of gods and buddhas are divine-way practices. More than that — your devout faith will itself obtain a deity-seed.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '烧香跪拜念经诵号，不是为了让你锻炼什么恒心，香火供奉的借口。入了那个坑，就走了神道路子，修到顶就是神佛分身，永远错失真道。', en: 'Burning incense, kneeling, chanting sutras and reciting names — these are not for training your perseverance; they are the incense-fire offering\'s pretext. Once in that pit, you are on the divine-way road; practice to the top and you are a god-buddha avatar — forever missing the true Way.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '并不是宗教里面存不存在这种说法，像这种事实肯定是不能说的，而且他们自己也未必懂。你只要信，身心就逐渐被下了神佛种子或者自生神佛种子，就不是你自身意愿可以左右的了。【不排除有的人已经察觉到了，至少我就知道有人已经擦绝到，并且在想办法弄掉。】', en: 'It is not a question of whether such a teaching exists within religion; facts like this certainly cannot be told, and they themselves may not understand it. As long as you believe, body and mind are gradually planted with a god-buddha seed or generate one themselves — no longer within the power of your own will to sway. [I do not rule out that some have sensed it; I for one know of people who have caught wind of it and are looking for ways to get rid of it.]' },
      { t: 'p', text: '无论是崇拜产生链接还是借用法力产生链接，你的精气神核心或者修炼核心就会变成神佛祖师的，通过修炼慢慢壮大这个核心，而属于你自己的越来越少，你的思维也会收到主动或者被动的影响，最终趋于同化，最后你还有一定自主意识，但核心神魂都不完全属于自己控制了。', en: 'Whether the link forms through worship or through borrowing dharma-power, your core of essence-qi-spirit — your core of practice — becomes the gods\', buddhas\' and patriarchs\'. Practice slowly swells that core; what belongs to you steadily shrinks. Your thought is influenced actively and passively, tending toward assimilation; in the end you still have some self-awareness, but the core spirit-soul is no longer wholly under your own control.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '当然祖师成就的，祖师可能是善良的不会收回，但根本上不由自主是事实。神佛在不缺香火的时候让你有一定自由，真需要的时候直接就收回分身了。', en: 'Of course, when it is the patriarch\'s accomplishment, the patriarch may be kind and not reclaim it — but that one is not master in one\'s own house is, at root, a fact. Gods and buddhas grant you a measure of freedom while incense-fire is plentiful; when they truly need you, the avatar is simply recalled.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '但是借助于神佛或者祖师神气的这种修炼要比纯自力修炼容易很多，所以有好多人自愿被下种、灌顶。', en: 'But this practice by the spirit-qi of gods, buddhas or patriarchs is far easier than pure self-power, so many volunteer for seed-planting and empowerment.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '毕竟大多数人看来，就算不由自主，也比灰飞烟火强。何况上面有人拉一把，比自力成功率高太多了。所以我其实是理解入神道的人士的，在搞明白道理的基础上，由自己去选择道路。反正都是为了修炼，虽然选择不同，都可以理解，但不支持。', en: 'After all, in most people\'s eyes, even unfreedom beats scattering like ash and smoke. And with someone above pulling you up, the success rate far exceeds self-power. So I in fact understand those who enter the divine way; having understood the reasoning, let each choose his own road. It is all for the sake of cultivation; different choices, all understandable — but not endorsed.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '有的人说，确实还有不信奉神灵，只信三清、祖师，和鬼神属于合作关系的。但是非常少，个别门派会有那么几个人走这条路。道教开始也不信神，现在是信神的多，毕竟大部分就是当成个职业，赚点香火钱混日子，没几个真学老庄信修炼的。胡教也一样，谈佛法的多，真修佛法的不多。', en: 'Some say there are indeed those who do not worship deities but trust only the Three Pure Ones and the patriarchs, holding a relation of cooperation with ghosts and gods. But they are very few — a handful in certain sects walk this road. Daoism in its beginning did not believe in gods either; now believers in gods are many — most take it as a profession, earning a bit of incense-money to get by; few truly study Laozi and Zhuangzi or believe in cultivation. The foreign faith is the same: many talk of the Buddha-dharma, few truly practice it.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '下种、灌顶的，大多是神佛祖师通过师父给你种的，不用感召直接给了种子，比感召的种子还要厉害许多。要么通过拜神、读经，也有的通过仪式获取。最容易得到的就是通过虔诚信仰，慢慢就召致了。稍微虔诚一点的信徒，感召神佛或者护法的分神入体，就是神佛种子。有的人被影响之后，就会从认可自力，改成深度信佛。有些人的固执，真不一定是有多大执念，这就是潜意识影响。不在乎的话，也不影响吃喝拉撒，其实你无法改变现状，你可以尝试接受现状。你认可它存在，不是还能练习请神上身嘛。', en: 'Seed-planting and empowerment are mostly done for you by gods, buddhas and patriarchs through the master: the seed is given directly without summoning, and is far stronger than a summoned seed. Or one obtains it through worshipping gods, reading sutras, or through rituals. Easiest of all is to summon it slowly through devout faith: a slightly devout believer draws the divided spirit of a god, buddha or guardian into the body — that is the god-buddha seed. Some, once influenced, change from endorsing self-power to deep Buddhist belief. Some people\'s stubbornness is not necessarily a great fixation — it is subconscious influence. If you do not mind it, it need not interfere with eating, drinking, and the rest. You cannot change the situation as it stands; you might try accepting it. You acknowledge it exists — can you not still practice inviting gods to mount the body?' },
      { t: 'p', text: '丹道之中，就有神道丹法，生前有一定成就的话，死后可以成为上神的属神属官。像有的号称纯无为法，他们讲的无为就是一味静坐，自力的话，是不可能成功的。他们平时修炼，本质就是用自己的神气去养那个种子，那个种子就是高层次的精神。甚至有的不用按丹道次第修炼，只要养分够了就培养出来了。也有些按自力的丹道次第辛苦修持，但最终因为沾染种子或信仰，只能走成为属神的道路的，可怜。', en: 'Within elixir-path there is divine-way elixir practice: with certain attainments in life, after death one may become a subordinate god or official of a higher god. Some claim to be pure non-action methods — their non-action is simply sitting in stillness; by self-power it is impossible to succeed. Their ordinary practice is in essence feeding that seed with their own spirit-qi; the seed is a high-level spirit. Some need not even follow the elixir grades — with enough nourishment it is raised. And some toil by the self-power elixir grades, yet in the end, tainted by seed or belief, can only walk the road of becoming a subordinate god — pitiable.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '只要信神信佛，也就成了半自力半神道，最终归于神道。佛法本身是可以修的，但不能信佛，不能信受奉行。修是修信是信，半点不可搭界。自力和神道没有中间路线，要么不沾香火或不畏香火，但凡你沾上一点，就会堕入神道。', en: 'To believe in gods and buddhas is already half self-power, half divine way — and in the end it comes to the divine way. The Buddha-dharma itself can be practiced, but one must not believe in the Buddha, must not accept and uphold it in faith. Practice is practice, faith is faith; the two must not touch by a hair. Between self-power and the divine way there is no middle road: either do not touch incense-fire, or do not fear it — touch it ever so little, and you fall into the divine way.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '禅宗那些老祖们搞呵佛骂祖，你以为搞着玩呢？那是为了破心中佛，破佛方能成佛，就算是我们普通人不信佛，心里也还有个佛，觉得他很伟大。你修佛法就会受这个影响，所以就要通过呵佛骂祖破掉他。你看那个倩女幽魂电影，里面就契合了这个道理，明明知道国师变的佛是假的，就是不能向佛出手。这就叫，破庙中佛易，破心中佛难。', en: 'The old patriarchs of Chan scolding the Buddha and cursing the ancestors — do you take that for play? It was to break the Buddha in the heart; only breaking the Buddha can one become Buddha. Even we ordinary people, not believing in the Buddha, still have a Buddha in the heart, thinking him very great. Practicing the Buddha-dharma, you will be influenced by this, so one must break him by scolding Buddha and cursing ancestors. In the film A Chinese Ghost Story this truth fits exactly: knowing full well that the Buddha the National Preceptor turned into is false, one still cannot raise a hand against the Buddha. This is called: breaking the Buddha in a temple is easy; breaking the Buddha in the heart is hard.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '修法术的那些更是脱离不了神道，生前使唤兵马，死后做兵马被人使唤。神佛鬼，他们的每一分法力都是他们灵魂的一部分，都是他们的分灵，所以借法借来的是什么？修法力修来的是什么？想想就知道了。你们有些人性情大变可能。说起来人的思维时刻受外界影响，不受这里影响，也受那里影响，就是影响的深浅不同，独立思考能力不同。', en: 'Those who practice magic arts are still less able to leave the divine way: in life they command the soldier-horses; in death they become soldier-horses commanded. Gods, buddhas and ghosts — every fraction of their dharma-power is a part of their soul, a divided spirit of theirs. So what is it you borrow when you borrow dharma? What do you cultivate when you cultivate dharma-power? Think, and you will know. Some of you may change greatly in temperament. Come to that, the human mind is at every moment influenced from outside — if not from here, then from there; only the depth of influence differs, and the strength of independent thought.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '法界之中，天兵天将天使护法童子侍女神兽天马法器神兵甚至树木，都有可能是用各种信众的灵魂充做的，封官嘛，你只要飞升上去，自然有你一个位置，例如让你化作斑马给上级拉车。', en: 'In the dharma-realm, heaven-soldiers and heaven-generals, angels, guardians, acolyte boys, attendant maidens, divine beasts, heaven-horses, dharma-instruments, divine weapons — even trees — may all be filled from the souls of believers of every kind. Enfeoffment, after all: ascend, and a place is naturally yours — turned into a zebra, say, to pull a superior\'s carriage.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '封神授职是有编制的，有编制的警察鬼神，就能管理没编制的混混鬼神，免得混混们打砸抢。', en: 'Enfeoffment and office carry establishment: gods and ghosts on the establishment, as police, can manage the gangster gods and ghosts off it — lest the riffraff smash, loot and rob.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '有一些修神道的自己是知道利弊的，甚至有清晰完整的传承，但架不如它容易啊，吸引力大，还能混吃混喝赚钞票，这是人家做出的选择。人家清楚地做选择的也不傻的，怎么也是个死，活着拿了好处，死后延续了灵魂生命，有付出有回报，他不亏，只不是修道就是了。', en: 'Some on the divine-way path know the pros and cons themselves, and even possess a clear, complete transmission — but one cannot resist how easy it is: the pull is strong, with food and drink to freeload and money to earn; it is the choice they have made. Those who choose with open eyes are no fools either: death comes one way or another; in life they take the benefits, in death the soul-life continues — payment given, return received; they do not come out behind. It is only that this is not cultivating the Dao, that is all.' },
    ],
  },
  {
    blocks: [
      { t: 'p', text: '神道法修炼中有一种靠吃鬼修炼的，在这里顺便说一下。鬼死为聻，吃鬼太多，自身灵魂也会逐渐往聻的性质转化。', en: 'Among divine-way practices there is one that cultivates by eating ghosts — a word on it here by the way. A ghost\'s death is the jian; eat too many ghosts, and one\'s own soul gradually turns toward the jian\'s nature.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '修道人的精神越纯粹，往上走的道路越宽。', en: 'The purer the cultivator\'s spirit, the broader the road upward.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '炼罡已经是不得已而为之的事，何况炼煞，更何况香火念力。', en: 'Refining the gang energies is already a thing done only from necessity; how much more refining the sha; and more still, incense-fire mind-thought.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '对自力修炼来说香火有毒，断绝道途。', en: 'For self-power practice, incense-fire is poison; it severs the road.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '所以说神道相较于佛道自力修炼，是较为低级的，内行人称之为，堕入神道。', en: 'So the divine way, compared with the self-power practice of the Buddha-dao, is of a lower order — those in the know call it falling into the divine way.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '但是他比自力容易的多，舒服的多，还特别自信。', en: 'But it is far easier than self-power, far more comfortable — and especially self-assured.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '这聻，是什么样的性质？', en: 'This jian — what nature does it have?' },
      { t: 'p', text: '人中的疯子已经是不可理喻，鬼中的疯子可想而知。', en: 'A madman among the living is already beyond reason; a mad ghost is left to the imagination.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '这种影响在人有身体的时候是影响不太大的，但极难解决，一旦失去身体，一下子就完蛋了。在有大量香火供给的情况下可以缓解，但属于饮鸩止渴。', en: 'This influence matters little while one has a body, but it is extremely hard to resolve; once the body is lost, it is over at once. With a great supply of incense-fire it can be eased — but that is drinking poison to quench thirst.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '聻本来是趋于消散的，但因为有大量信力的补充，所以能够维持其存在。所以宗教内的人士还是可以靠吃鬼壮大魂魄的，无所谓的事。但这个方法和立教修神法一样存在重大缺陷，就是神形会分离，肉身会腐朽，修的越快，死的越快。', en: 'The jian tends by nature to dissipate, but with a great replenishment of faith-power it can maintain its existence. So those within religion can indeed swell their soul by eating ghosts — a matter of no consequence. But this method, like founding a religion to cultivate godhood, carries a grave defect: spirit and form separate, the body rots — the faster one practices, the faster one dies.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '总的来说就是，纯香火的，只靠传教有功，一口气上五楼不费劲，但自主性最小，成就了能力也小，法界职务也小。半自力但信奉神佛祖师，靠神佛祖师拉一把这种半神道，自主性更大，成就也高，但费力些。完全自力修炼完全自主，成就最高，但成功率最低。', en: 'In sum: the purely incense-fire kind, meritorious only through preaching, can carry you up five flights without gasping — but autonomy is least, the accomplishment gained small, the dharma-realm office small. The half self-power kind, believing in gods, buddhas and patriarchs, pulled up by them — this half divine way has greater autonomy and higher accomplishment, but costs more effort. Full self-power practice, fully autonomous, holds the highest accomplishment — and the lowest success rate.' },
      { t: 'p', text: '之所以给大家讲这些，就是让大家对神道能有一定的了解。明白清楚自己选择了什么', en: 'I set all this before you so that you may have some understanding of the divine way — knowing clearly what it is you have chosen.' },
    ],
  },
];
